# Data conversion between bit and tebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between bit and tebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1b to 0.0000TiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5b yields 0.0000TiB; backward, converting 1TiB to 8796093022208b preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5TiB yields 13194139533312.0b. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1b
print(forward_whole->to(TiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5b
print(forward_fractional->to(TiB))
backward_whole: int = 1TiB
print(backward_whole->to(b))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TiB
print(backward_fractional->to(b))

<<< stdout
0.0000TiB
0.0000TiB
8796093022208b
13194139533312.0b

<<< stderr
